from pathlib import Path
p=Path('experiments/20260905-bridge-length-phase-diagram/coordinator_report.md')
s=p.read_text().replace('Status: unresolved pending independent R3 audit.','Status: proved; independent R3 incidence audit accepted. Exact coordinator\\nchecks also passed through N=6,m=12.')
s+='''
## Coordinator candidate: obstruction to using only minimal components

Status: unresolved pending independent R3 audit.

Let m=2k>0, M_d=binom(d,2), and 2≤r≤N. For each labeled minimal
component of size v, the normalized count is v"'^(v−3), the number of
Cayley trees divided by v. Summing over support partitions therefore gives

```
Z0(N,2k)/(2k)! = sum_{forests F on [N], |E(F)|=k} product_{B component} 1/|B|
               ≤ binom(M_N,k).
```

The singleton factor is one. For even m, the return probability on S_r is
at least 2/r! by Cauchy–Schwarz at the midpoint on the reachable parity
class. Restricting every factor to a fixed r-set yields
`Z(N,m)≥2 M_r''^m/r!`. Thus

```
Z0/Z ≤ min(1, m! binom(M_N,m/2) r! / [2 M_r''^m]).
```

For m=2floor(theta N), fixed 0<theta<1, choose r=floor(N/log N).
Elementary factorial/binomial bounds give numerator log at most
`3theta N log N+O_theta(N)`, and denominator log at least
`4theta N log N−4theta N log log N−O_theta(N)`. Consequently

```
Z0/Z ≤ exp(−theta N log N+O_theta(N log log N)) → 0,
TV(U conditioned on total surplus zero,U) → 1.
```

For theta≥1 the minimal subset is eventually empty. This obstructs one
named sampler family only. It neither proves hardness at linear length nor
rules out positive-surplus primitives or the certified full hybrid.

## Additional focused literature reconciliation

Féray–Louf–Thévenin, [Corollary 1](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00440-022-01170-9),
gives asymptotically uniform fixed-genus factorizations of a long cycle.
The endpoint and length n−1+2g differ from the present connected identity
primitive at 2n−2+2g, and the statement is not a tunable accuracy guarantee.

DPS, [*Bijections for simple and double Hurwitz numbers*, Theorems 1 and 4](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1410.6521),
extends the correspondence to coherent higher-genus Hurwitz mobiles.
The inspected theorem does not provide the required polynomial sampler for
those coherent objects. This is a possible research route, not a discharged
sampling dependency.

The focused search also inspected Chapuy–Louf–Walsh,
[*Random Partitions Under the Plancherel–Hurwitz Measure, High Genus Hurwitz Numbers and Maps*](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.AofA.2022.6),
Theorem 5, because it counts exactly the identity words at linear length.
No claim here depends on its asymptotics; the elementary bound above is
sufficient for the minimal-only obstruction. These source checks do not
establish novelty or prove that no other sampler exists.
'"'''
p.write_text(s)
print('HEARTBEAT coordinator-checks=passed cells=78 sparse-incidence=accepted minimal-only-linear-obstruction=audit-pending')
