Completed in about **56 minutes**. Classification: **`quantified-phase-diagram`**. All three reports, fresh nonauthor audits, and final synthesis are complete.

The internally audited results establish:

- **Short:** exact sampling in \(\exp(O(\sqrt{\min(m,N)}))\operatorname{poly}(N,m)\) expected bit time, hence polynomial for \(m=O(\log^2N)\).
- **Sparse:** polynomial sampling with TV error at most \(m^4/[48(N-m+1)^2]\) for even \(m\le N\).
- **Dense:** for \(N\ge5\), polynomial expected-time, \(\epsilon\)-close sampling whenever feasible
  \[
  m\ge2N(N-1)\left\lceil144\ln(3N^2/\epsilon)\right\rceil.
  \]

Every output has the exact requested endpoint. An intermediate gap remains. Connected scalar counts are polynomial-time computable; connected positive-surplus word generation remains unresolved, beginning with genus one at length \(2v\). **No computational hardness result is claimed.**

